# Railway build context = repo root (the gateway Dockerfile builds from here). The image only
# COPYs pyproject.toml, uv.lock, services/*/{pyproject,src}, content/atom/pyproject.toml and the
# two runtime content files (content/catalogs/concepts.json, content/factbase/facts.v1.jsonl) — so
# everything else is dead upload weight. Excluding it drops the upload from ~630 MB to a few MB
# (the reason `railway up` was timing out mid-upload).

# --- Secrets: the gateway takes every value from Railway service variables at
# --- runtime. No env file may ever ride along in the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Weight ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
.git
**/dist
.vercel
.vercel/output
apps
packages
content/cache
# content/catalogs + content/factbase ride along on purpose (~2.7 MB): the gateway image
# COPYs concepts.json and facts.v*.jsonl out of them. Only the runtime cache is excluded.
.playwright-mcp
*.png
*.log
scratchpad
